        '3-5', $q$Hana and Bolt$q$, $q$The same author wrote both of these stories about the same two characters.

Text 1: Bolt Gets Lost

Bolt was a small robot in Room 12. Bolt could roll, beep and carry paper. One morning, Bolt rolled out the door to deliver a note to the office. But the hallway had many turns. Bolt beeped in a sad, low voice. Hana heard the beeping and found Bolt near the gym. Hana drew a simple map with arrows and taped it to Bolt's screen. Bolt followed the arrows and reached the office. Everyone in Room 12 cheered when Bolt rolled back.

Text 2: Bolt Saves the Day

On Friday, Hana could not find a library book. The book was due that afternoon. Hana looked in the desk, the backpack and the coat hook. Nothing. Then Bolt rolled over and beeped three times. Bolt's camera had seen the book on the reading rug during story time. Bolt led Hana to the rug, and there was the book under a pillow. Hana returned it to the library just in time. "Thanks, Bolt," Hana said. "Now we are even."$q$, 'draft')
