-- Passage rg3-connections-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('33cfed1a-afcb-5891-8b12-791fe3865987', 'rg3-connections-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-connections'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Bridge at Willow Creek$q$, $q$Long ago, the town of Willow Creek had no bridge. A wide river ran between the farms and the town market. Farmers crossed the river on a small wooden boat.

One spring, heavy rains made the river rise. The water moved too fast for the boat. For three weeks, farmers could not bring their eggs, corn and milk to the market. Families in town had less food to buy. The farmers lost money because they could not sell their goods.

After the river went down, the people of Willow Creek held a town meeting. They agreed that the town needed a bridge. Each family gave a little money. Some people gave time instead. They cut logs, carried stones and hauled sand.

The work took two summers. First, workers built strong stone pillars in the river. Then they laid thick logs across the pillars. Last, they nailed boards on top to make a flat path.

When the bridge opened, farmers could cross the river any day of the year. More food came to the market, so prices went down. The town grew, too. New families moved to Willow Creek because it was now easy to travel there. Years later, the people built a school right next to the bridge.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
