-- Passage rg3-literary-structure-pov-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('001ce50e-89dc-54c8-aed4-5cb59fc9bc51', 'rg3-literary-structure-pov-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Swings for Elm Park: A Play$q$, $q$Scene 1

(Saturday morning. A sunny sidewalk. KOFI and AUNT DELIA set up a table with a pitcher and paper cups.)

KOFI: Today we will raise money for new swings at Elm Park!

AUNT DELIA: How many cups do you think we will sell?

KOFI: At least a hundred. Everyone loves lemonade.

(An hour passes. People walk by, but no one stops.)

KOFI: Nobody is thirsty. This is the worst idea ever.

AUNT DELIA: Maybe people do not know why we are here.

KOFI: Then let's tell them! (KOFI grabs a marker and a big sheet of paper.)

Scene 2

(The same sidewalk, that afternoon. A sign on the table says SWINGS FOR ELM PARK in giant letters.)

JOGGER: (stopping to read the sign) New swings for the park? I will take two cups, please.

(Soon a line of neighbors stretches down the sidewalk.)

KOFI: Aunt Delia, we sold forty cups!

AUNT DELIA: That is not a hundred, Kofi.

KOFI: I know. But every cup gets the swings a little closer. This was my best idea ever!$q$, 'draft')
