-- Passage rg3-literary-structure-pov-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('ae9178c1-0297-5794-aec0-7feb929d6d72', 'rg3-literary-structure-pov-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Old Schoolhouse$q$, $q$Our class was visiting the Hollow Creek Schoolhouse Museum. I was sure it would be the most boring trip ever. "It is just an old room with old desks," I told my friend Priya.

Inside, a guide named Mr. Osei handed each of us a small slate and a stick of chalk. "This is how children did their lessons long ago," he said. There was no paper. If you made a mistake, you wiped the slate with a rag.

Then Mr. Osei rang a brass bell. We stood up straight and said our times tables out loud, all together. Priya giggled, and so did I. It felt like we had traveled back in time.

Next, Mr. Osei showed us a tin lunch pail. He said some students walked three miles to school, even in snow. I thought about my bus ride. It only takes ten minutes.

On the bus home, Priya asked what I thought of the trip. "It was okay," I said. Then I smiled. "Maybe old rooms are not so boring after all." I held my slate in my lap the whole way home.$q$, 'draft')
