-- Passage rg3-literary-structure-pov-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('2e43eac8-2497-5e8f-9d34-7a8d06091bed', 'rg3-literary-structure-pov-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Rain Jar: A Play$q$, $q$Scene 1

(Monday afternoon. A backyard with a bare patch of dirt. NOOR holds a packet of tomato seeds. GRANDPA AMIR holds an empty glass jar and a ruler.)

NOOR: Let's plant the seeds right now!

GRANDPA AMIR: First we should learn how much rain falls here. We will make a rain jar.

(GRANDPA AMIR tapes the ruler to the side of the jar. NOOR sets the jar in the middle of the yard.)

NOOR: (sighing) This will take forever. I want to plant today.

GRANDPA AMIR: Good gardeners watch first, then plant.

Scene 2

(Thursday morning, after a big storm. The yard is wet. A puddle covers the low corner of the dirt patch.)

NOOR: (lifting the jar) Grandpa, look! The water reaches the two on the ruler. Two whole inches!

GRANDPA AMIR: And look at that corner. It is still flooded.

NOOR: If we had planted there on Monday, the seeds would be swimming!

GRANDPA AMIR: So where should the tomatoes go?

NOOR: (pointing) On the high side, where the dirt is dry. Watching first was a smart idea.$q$, 'draft')
