-- Passage rg3-literary-structure-pov-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('a75d7957-1e8f-5718-9ee9-c5a8b688084f', 'rg3-literary-structure-pov-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Mural Wall$q$, $q$Chapter 1: Two Ideas

Ms. Bello's class was going to paint a mural on the wall beside the town library. Ravi raised a hand first. "Let's paint the ocean, with whales and bright fish!" Yuki frowned. "No, let's paint our city, with tall buildings and the bridge." The two friends argued until the bell rang. Ms. Bello said, "Come back tomorrow with one plan."

Chapter 2: One Plan

The next day, Ravi and Yuki sat at a table with paper and crayons. Ravi drew waves. Yuki drew buildings. Then Yuki stopped. "Wait. Our city is right next to the bay." Ravi grinned. "So the water can go at the bottom, and the buildings can stand behind it!" They drew boats in the harbor and a whale splashing near the bridge.

Chapter 3: Painting Day

On Saturday, the whole class painted. Ravi mixed blues for the water. Yuki painted windows on the buildings. A man walking his dog stopped to look. "A city by the sea," he said. "It looks like the best of both."

Ravi and Yuki looked at each other and laughed.$q$, 'draft')
