insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('8244593f-5dda-598b-9618-c98de7b1b8a2', 'rg3-text-structure-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-text-structure'), null,
        '3-5', $q$How Maple Creek Got Its Library$q$, $q$The town of Maple Creek did not always have a library. This is the story of how it got one.

Heading: 1910, Books in a Store

At first, the town had no library building. A shop owner named Mr. Okafor kept a shelf of books near the front window. Neighbors could borrow a book for one week.

Heading: 1925, A Growing Collection

Later, more people wanted to read. The shelf grew to fill a whole back room. Families gave books they had already read. Soon there were more than five hundred books.

Heading: 1938, A New Building

The back room became too crowded. So the town held bake sales and fairs to raise money. After three years of saving, workers built a brick library on Main Street.

Heading: Today

Now the Maple Creek Library has computers, story time and a garden for reading outside. About two hundred people visit each day.

Timeline in words: 1910, book shelf in a store. 1925, back room fills with books. 1938, brick library opens. Today, computers and story time.

Picture caption: Children sit on the library steps on opening day in 1938.

Index: bake sales, see 1938. computers, see Today. Mr. Okafor, see 1910. story time, see Today.$q$, 'draft')
