insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('c530fd03-99cb-592b-b5be-853a8d17b9b6', 'rg3-text-structure-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-text-structure'), null,
        '3-5', $q$From Bottle to Jacket$q$, $q$Did you know that an old plastic bottle can become a warm jacket? Here is how it happens.

Heading: Collecting

First, people put empty bottles in a recycling bin. A truck takes the bottles to a recycling center. Workers sort them so that only clear plastic bottles are kept.

Heading: Cleaning and Chopping

Next, machines wash the bottles and peel off the labels. Then the bottles are chopped into tiny pieces called flakes. The flakes look like bits of confetti.

Heading: Melting and Spinning

After that, the flakes are melted into a thick, gooey liquid. A machine pushes the liquid through very small holes. The liquid comes out as long, thin threads, like spaghetti. The threads cool and harden.

Heading: Making the Cloth

Last, the threads are stretched, fluffed and knitted into a soft, fuzzy cloth called fleece. A factory cuts and sews the fleece into jackets.

Sidebar, Did You Know?: It can take about twenty-five bottles to make one fleece jacket.

Glossary: flakes, small chopped pieces of plastic. fleece, a soft, fuzzy cloth. recycling, using old things to make new things.$q$, 'draft')
