   $q$What is the central message of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Dogs do not like loud music in the house.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-lesson"},{"text":"Harmonicas are too hard for children to learn to play.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Always let an older sister fix your problems for you.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character-role"},{"text":"Mistakes can show you how to get better, so keep practicing.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mistakes can show you how to get better, so keep practicing.$q$, $q$Kai learns something from each noisy try, practices, and plays the song on Sunday. Rosa only asks a question; Kai does the practicing, so the story is not about letting someone else fix the problem.$q$, 'draft', 'b51b3bc0-42c2-5985-b621-f0648f8f9fc4')
