   $q$In the fourth stanza, the rain "sounded like a picnic song." What does this show about the speaker?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker's feelings have changed, so even the rain now seems cheerful.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker wants to go back outside and sing in the rain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The speaker thinks the rain is too loud to hear the story.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The speaker is still upset that the picnic was not at the park.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker's feelings have changed, so even the rain now seems cheerful.$q$, $q$Earlier the rain made the day feel "ruined," but now it sounds like a song, which shows the change that carries the message. Nothing says the speaker wants to go outside.$q$, 'draft', '45e8d202-b39c-500e-a702-bdbe2cec142c')
