   $q$What is the author's main point?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Water wheels were the most important invention in early towns.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Towns grew beside rivers because rivers gave them what they needed.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Rivers often flooded in spring and made life hard for towns.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-evidence"},{"text":"Today, people no longer need rivers for anything at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Towns grew beside rivers because rivers gave them what they needed.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says rivers "gave early towns many of the things they needed to grow," and the rest gives reasons. Water wheels are only one of those reasons.$q$, 'draft', 'f4ef9bd8-0f01-504e-9f38-09b1906450fb')
