   $q$Why is Ruth's diary entry a firsthand account?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ruth tells the year that the first telephone came to town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"facts-mean-firsthand"},{"text":"Ruth heard about the telephone later from Father.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Ruth read about the telephone on a sign at the museum.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-firsthand-secondhand"},{"text":"Ruth was in the store and turned the telephone crank by hand.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ruth was in the store and turned the telephone crank by hand.$q$, $q$Ruth writes, "Mr. Hollis let me turn the little crank," so Ruth was there. The museum sign was made much later and is the secondhand account.$q$, 'draft', '064323a2-28fb-55e8-b4e2-3583476ca071')
