-- Passage rg4-comparing-texts-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('2a160408-a950-5c64-9826-5843d3edde0a', 'rg4-comparing-texts-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Honest Choice$q$, $q$Text 1: The Extra Coin (a story from Egypt)

Karim helped his uncle sell oranges at the market in Cairo. One busy morning, a woman paid for a bag of oranges and hurried away. When Karim counted the coins, he saw she had given him too much.

Karim could have kept the extra coin. No one would know. Instead, he grabbed it and ran through the crowd. "Ma'am, wait!" he called. He found her near the bread stall and gave the coin back.

The woman smiled. The next week, she came back and bought three bags of oranges. "I only shop," she said, "where people are honest."

Text 2: The Fisher's Net (a poem from Scotland)

Old Morag mends her nets
beside the harbor wall.
A careless boat drifts in
and bumps her pile of nets.

The young man at the wheel
could sail off fast and hide.
But he climbs out instead
and says, "That fault was mine."

He helps her mend each hole
until the sun goes down.
Now every time he sails in,
she waves him safely home.$q$, 'draft')
